"Though of primitive craftsmanship, the great weight of this weapon's blade gives it excellent striking power."
msgstr ""
"En dépit d’une fabrication primitive, la masse considérable de la lame de cette arme lui confère une excellente puissance de frappe."

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:5
msgid "Trollish War Sword"
msgstr "Epée de guerre trollienne"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:50
msgid ""
"A versatile weapon combining the qualities of an axe and a spear, the halberd is designed to perform in formation and individual close quarter fighting."
msgstr ""
"Arme polyvalente associant les qualités d’une hache et d’une lance, la hallebarde est conçue pour manœuvrer en formation et se battre au corps à corps."

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:502
msgid "book 499"
msgstr "livre 499"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:503
msgid ""
"(Accuracy +40, 10-20 points of Light damage) The Forge of Chaos was destroyed in the making of the Swords of Balance. Legend says the Blade of Light, Elsenrail, and the Blade of Dark, Glomenthal, will play major roles in the last act of the universe."
msgstr ""
"(Précision +40, 10-20 points de dégâts de la Lumière) La Forge du chaos a été détruite pendant la fabrication des Epées de l’équilibre. Selon la légende, la Lame de la lumière, Elsenrail, et la Lame de l’ombre, Glomenthal, joueront des rôles majeurs dans le dernier acte de l’univers."

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:503 assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:504
msgid "Artifact Longsword"
msgstr "Epée"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:503
msgid "Elsenrail"
msgstr "Elsenrail"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:504
msgid ""
"(Might +40, 10-20 points of Dark damage) The Forge of Chaos was destroyed in the making of the Swords of Balance. Legend says the Blade of Light, Elsenrail, and the Blade of Dark, Glomenthal, will play major roles in the last act of the universe."
msgstr ""
"(Force +40, 10-20 points de dégâts de l’Ombre) La Forge du chaos a été détruite pendant la fabrication des Epées de l’équilibre. Selon la légende, la Lame de la lumière, Elsenrail, et la Lame de l’ombre, Glomenthal, joueront des rôles majeurs dans le dernier acte de l’univers."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:504
msgid "Glomenthal"
msgstr "Glomenthal"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:505
msgid ""
"(Armsmaster skill +7, Air Resistance +30) As a child, before he carved his barbarian kingdom in Vori, Lars Eilief found this sword deep in an ice cave. When he died, it was set adrift with him on his funeral barge. How it ended up in Jadame is a mystery."
msgstr ""
"(Compétence Maître d’armes +7, Protection contre l’Air +30) Enfant, avant de conquérir son royaume barbare à Vori, Lars Eilief trouva cette épée au fond d’une grotte de glace. A la mort de Lars, on a fait partir l’épée à la dérive avec lui sur sa barge funéraire. On ne sait pas comment elle est arrivée à Jadame."

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:505
msgid "Artifact Broadsword"
msgstr "Glaive"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:505
msgid "Terminus"
msgstr "Terminus"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:506
msgid ""
"(Endurance +40, Luck +40, Ogre Slaying) Before there was a Regnan Empire, the ancestors of the Trolls of Ironsand lived on Regna Island. With this blade and a horde of sea raiders, Hareck I ousted the Trolls and formed his pirate nation."
msgstr ""
"(Endurance +40, Chance +40, Massacre d’ogres) Avant l’existence de l’empire regnan, les ancêtres des trolls du Désert du sable de fer vivaient dans l’île de Regna. Avec l’aide de cette lame et une horde d’écumeurs des mers, Hareck Ier expulsa les trolls et forma sa nation pirate."

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:506
msgid "Artifact Cutlass"
msgstr "Coutelas"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:506
msgid "Judicious Measure"
msgstr "Mesure judicieuse"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:507
msgid ""
"(Might +20, Swift, 6-12 points of Cold damage, Minotaur) When the Dark Dwarves carved the first Minotaur labyrinth into the heart of Mt. Ashenbane they forged this axe for Xaxius, the first herdmaster."
msgstr ""
"(Force +20, Rapidité, 6-12 points de dégâts du Froid, Minotaure) Lorsque les nains de l’Ombre creusèrent le premier labyrinthe des minotaures au cœur du Mont Ashenbane, ils forgèrent cette hache pour Xaxius, premier maître de troupe."

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:507
msgid "Artifact Axe"
msgstr "Hache"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:507
msgid "Elderaxe"
msgstr "Hache de l’Aîné"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:508
msgid ""
"(10-20 points of Fire damage, Fire Resistance +40) The mad artificer, Cornelius of Blackshire, built this axe for the purpose of clearing the trees around his country estate. \"A single blow will both fell a tree and render it into firewood!\" he was heard to exclaim. That he was soon found slain and the axe gone missing is proof that someone saw a better use for the tool."
msgstr ""
"(10-20 points de dégâts du Feu, Protection contre le Feu +40) L’artificier fou, Cornelius de Blackshire, fabriqua cette hache pour abattre les arbres autour de sa propriété. “ Un seul coup suffit pour abattre un arbre et le débiter en bois de chauffage ! ”, l’entendit-on s’exclamer. Peu après, on le découvrit assassiné et la hache avait disparu. De toute évidence, quelqu’un avait trouvé une meilleure utilisation pour cet outil."

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:508
msgid "Artifact Two-Handed Axe"
msgstr "Hache à deux mains"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/english/Global.txt:559 assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:508
msgid "Volcano"
msgstr "Volcan"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:509
msgid ""
"(Endurance +20, Dragon Slaying, Swift) Arguably the best dragon hunter of all times, Sir Ryan Smedly carried this mighty spear with him on all his expeditions, claiming that with it in hand, he could best any dragon in single combat. This proved true, but nevertheless he was slain by no less than a dozen dragons who ambushed him at Shadowmarsh Pass."
msgstr ""
"(Endurance +20, Massacre de dragons, Rapidité) Sans doute le meilleur chasseur de dragons de tous les temps, Sire Ryan Smedly emportait cette lance puissante dans toutes ses expéditions. Selon lui, elle lui permettait de battre n’importe quel dragon en combat singulier. Et il n’avait pas tort. Il fut néanmoins tué par une douzaine de dragons, pas moins. Ceux-ci lui avaient tendu une embuscade au Passage des marais de l’Obscurité."

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:509
msgid "Artifact Spear"
msgstr "Lance"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:509
msgid "Wyrm Spitter"
msgstr "Broche à dragons"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:51
msgid "Beaked Halberd"
msgstr "Hallebarde à crochet"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:51
msgid ""
"This improved halberd has a spiked blade opposite its axe face to provide both balance and a means of penetrating plate armor."
msgstr ""
"Cette hallebarde améliorée comporte un fer pointu du côté opposé à la hache, à la fois pour équilibrer l’arme et fournir un moyen de pénétrer les armures articulées."

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:510
msgid ""
"(+10 to all attributes, 10-20 points of Body damage) The great Vampire, Korbu was known to use living men to guard his crypt during daylight hours. Compelled by a spell of enslavement, these sorry souls would walk their rounds carrying these mighty halberds. When Korbu mysteriously vanished, and the slave spell failed, a few of these weapons appeared in the larger world."
msgstr ""
"(+10 à tous les attributs, 10-20 points de dégâts par le Corps) Korbu, le grand vampire, était connu pour faire garder sa crypte par des hommes pendant la journée. Possédées par un sort d’esclavage, ces pauvres âmes faisaient leurs rondes en portant ces puissantes hallebardes. Après la mystérieuse disparition de Korbu, le sort d’esclavage fut rompu. Quelques-unes de ces armes firent alors leur apparition dans d’autres contrées."

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:510
msgid "Artifact Halberd"
msgstr "Hallebarde"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/english/Global.txt:460 assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:510
msgid "Guardian"
msgstr "Gardienne"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:511
msgid ""
"(Vampiric, 10 points of Poison damage, Vampire) At the conclusion of the Vampires' War of the Chalice, Korbu exacted horrific retribution on his defeated enemy, Calden Fain. It is better for the world that knowledge of the necromantic arts which rendered Fain--body and soul--into this living blade, is lost."
msgstr ""
"(Vampirique, 10 points de dégâts de poison, Vampire) A la fin de la Guerre vampirique du calice, Korbu fit subir une horrible vengeance à son ennemi vaincu, Calden Fain. La connaissance des arts nécromanciens à l’origine de la transformation de Fain en cette lame vivante s’est volatilisée. Tant mieux !"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:511
msgid "Artifact Long Dagger"
msgstr "Dague longue"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:511
msgid "Foulfang"
msgstr "Foulfang"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:512
msgid ""
"(Personality + 40, Regenerate Hit Points) Uri Hossana, King of the Western Elves, also called \"The Drunken King,\" was deposed the day he carelessly misplaced his scepter of office while on a hunting trip. This proved to be the last blunder of an incapable ruler. His advisors relieved him of his crown and left him to fend for himself in the Howling Marsh. He was never seen again."
msgstr ""
"(Personnalité +40, restaure les points de santé) Uri Hossana, Roi des elfes d’Occident, également appelé “ le Roi ivre ”, fut détrôné le jour où il égara son sceptre de fonction lors d’une partie de chasse. Ce fut la dernière gaffe d’un souverain incapable. Ses conseillers lui retirèrent sa couronne et l’abandonnèrent dans le Marais hurlant. On ne l’a jamais revu."

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:512
msgid "Artifact Mace"
msgstr "Masse"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:512
msgid "Scepter of Kings"
msgstr "Sceptre des rois"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:513
msgid ""
"(Might +20, Endurance +20, 10-20 points of Body damage) Trollish folklore is full of the fables of Sevenstrong Burlfist who with Biter, his faithful wolf companion, and his mighty club, Breaker, endlessly quested for the Silver Rose. Fables? One must wonder, if Breaker exists, then why not too, the Silver Rose?"
msgstr ""
"(Force +20, Endurance +20, 10-20 points de dégâts par le Corps) Le folklore trollien est riche de fables de Sevenstrong Burlfist. Avec Mordeur, son fidèle loup, et Casseur, sa puissante massue, il rechercha sans fin la Rose d’argent. Des fables ? On ne peut s’empêcher de se demander : “ Si Casseur existe, pourquoi pas aussi la Rose d’argent ? ”"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:513
msgid "Artifact Club"
msgstr "Massue"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:513
msgid "Breaker"
msgstr "Casseur"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:514
msgid ""
"(of Shielding; Immune to disease, paralysis, and poison) Nemerit, an otherwise unremarkable witch of the last era, was renown for her staff artificing skill. She created a staff for every conceivable use. It is said she carried this staff on reagent collecting trips into the swamplands."
msgstr ""
"(de bouclier ; Immunise contre la maladie, la paralysie et le poison) Sorcière de la dernière ère, Nemerit, par ailleurs peu remarquable, était renommée pour sa compétence d’artificière, appliquée aux bâtons. Elle créa un bâton pour chaque utilisation imaginable. On raconte qu’elle portait ce bâton-ci pour aller chercher des réactifs dans les marécages."

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:514
msgid "Artifact Staff"
msgstr "Bâton"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:514
msgid "Staff of the Swamp"
msgstr "Bâton des marécages"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:515
msgid ""
"(Accuracy +50, Swift, Bow skill +4) Legends tell of many great archer heroes, but none greater than Brennan Morland of whom it was said once pierced a gold sovereign at 300 paces in an archery tournament. Now, holding his bow you must wonder if the legend owes more to the bow than the man."
msgstr ""
"(Précision +50, Rapidité, compétence Arc +4) Les légendes mentionnent nombre de grands archers héroïques, mais le plus grand de tous reste Brennan Morland. Il aurait percé un souverain d’or à 300 pas lors d’un tournoi de tir à l’arc. Avec son arc entre les mains, vous devez vous demander si la légende tient davantage de l’arc que de l’homme."

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:515
msgid "Artifact Bow"
msgstr "Arc"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:515
msgid "Longseeker"
msgstr "Longseeker"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:516
msgid ""
"(Regenerates Spell Points, Endurance +30) A mage known as much for frailty of body as for magical prowess, Serendine of Freehaven built this armor to make the most of his strengths and the least of his weaknesses."
msgstr ""
"(Restaure les points de sort, Endurance +30) Mage connu pour sa fragilité physique et ses prouesses magiques, Serendine de Freehaven fabriqua cette armure pour tirer le maximum de ses forces et amoindrir ses faiblesses."

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:516
msgid "Artifact Leather Armor"
msgstr "Armure en cuir"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:516
msgid "Serendine's Preservation"
msgstr "Préservation de Serendine"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:517
msgid ""
"(+10 to all statistics, +10 to all resistances, Dark Elf) Dark and Light Elven dealings have been peaceable, if uneasy, for centuries. Before that there was nothing but war. Few suits of this Dark Elven war armor have survived the ravages of time. Those that have are understandably, coveted."
msgstr ""
"(+10 dans toutes les statistiques, +10 dans toutes les protections, Elfe de l’Ombre) Houleuses, les relations entre les elfes de l’Ombre et de la Lumière ont su rester pacifiques pendant des siècles. Avant cela, c’était la guerre. Peu d’armures ont survécu aux ravages de cette guerre des elfes de l’Ombre. Les quelques-unes restantes sont bien sûr très prisées."

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:517
msgid "Artifact Chainmail"
msgstr "Cotte de mailles"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:517
msgid "Glomenmail"
msgstr "Glomenmaille"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:518
msgid ""
"(Swift, +15 Speed, +15 Accuracy, Knight) Each grandmaster of the Blackshire Armorers' Guild creates a masterpiece suit of plate as proof of his right to hold his station. It is not unusual for a guild member to spend ten to twenty years in the creation of one of these suits."
msgstr ""
"(Rapidité, +15 en Vitesse, +15 en Précision, Chevalier) Chaque grand maître de la Guilde des armuriers de Blackshire crée une armure articulée, véritable chef-d’œuvre, pour prouver qu’il mérite son rang. Dix à vingt années seront souvent nécessaires pour créer l’une des ces armures."

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:518
msgid "Artifact Plate Armor"
msgstr "Armure articulée (plaques)"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:518
msgid "Supreme Plate"
msgstr "Armure suprême"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:519
msgid "Artifact Large Shield"
msgstr "Grand bouclier"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:519
msgid ""
"Quest Item: (of Spirit, of Body, of Mind, Cleric) When the First Temple of the Sun was burned in the War of Dove and Crow fought between the Sun and Moon temples, the holy altar was melted. The altar's metal was later collected and incorporated into this shield carried by Sun Priest Derico during his final deciding campaign of the war."
msgstr ""
"Objet de quête : (de Spiritisme, de Corps, d’Esprit, Clerc) le Premier Temple du Soleil fut brûlé lors de la Guerre de la colombe et du corbeau entre les Temples du Soleil et de la Lune. L’autel sacré fondit dans l’incendie. Le métal de l’autel fut ramassé et incorporé dans ce bouclier porté par Derico, prêtre du Temple du Soleil, pendant sa dernière campagne décisive."

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:52
msgid "Minotaur Campaign Pole-axe"
msgstr "Arme d’hast de campagne de minotaure"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:52
msgid ""
"When the Minotaurs went to war with the Frost Giants of faraway Vori, their king Balthazar commissioned this polearm to arm his troops. He reportedly said, \"Since they will be gone so long, arm them with something versatile.\""
msgstr ""
"Lorsque les minotaures sont partis en guerre contre les géants du Gel de la lointaine contrée de Vori, leur roi Balthazar a commandé cette arme d’hast pour ses troupes. Il aurait déclaré : “ Puisqu’ils partent pour si longtemps, donnez-leur une arme polyvalente. ”"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:520
msgid ""
"(+8 to Disarm Trap, Bow, and Armsmaster skills) That she would actually have a name for her gloves, is evidence of the flamboyant, if deserved, conceit of Darcie Darby--most widely known for her theft of the bejeweled Rod of Right, part of the royal regalia of Enroth."
msgstr ""
"(+8 aux compétences Désamorcer, Arc et Maître d’armes) Que ses gants portent un nom est la preuve de la vanité flamboyante, bien que méritée, de Darcie Darby, célèbre pour son vol de la Baguette du bien, élément de la parure royale d’Enroth."

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1339 assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:520
msgid "Artifact Gauntlets"
msgstr "Gantelets"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:520
msgid "Fleetfingers"
msgstr "Doigts de fée"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:521
msgid ""
"(Speed + 30, Swift, Immunity to Sleep) When Jerico Ironfist secured the throne in the First War of Enrothian Succession, he sent forth heralds to spread the news. They were given pairs of these boots so the news would be spread quickly and thus soonest end widespread civil unrest."
msgstr ""
"(Vitesse +30, Rapidité, Immunité contre le sommeil) Après sa prise du trône lors de la Première Guerre de succession d’Enroth, Jerico Ironfist envoya des messagers annoncer la nouvelle. Pour mettre fin le plus tôt possible à l’agitation générale, on leur remit une paire de ces bottes afin que la nouvelle soit répandue rapidement."

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:521
msgid "Artifact Boots"
msgstr "Bottes"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:521
msgid "Herald's Boots"
msgstr "Bottes de messager"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:522
msgid ""
"(+40 to Fire, Earth, Water and Air resistances) When the cartographer Alvia Morrania went to chart the terrain of the elemental planes she went well prepared. This ring of general protection was among the many special items commissioned by the Enrothian courts in support of her expedition."
msgstr ""
"(+40 en Protection contre le Feu, la Terre, l’Eau et l’Air) La cartographe Alvia Morrania s’était bien préparée pour aller repérer les Mondes des élémentaires. Cet anneau de protection générale faisait partie des nombreux objets spécialement commandés par les tribunaux d’Enroth en soutien à son expédition."

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1341 assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:522
msgid "Artifact Ring"
msgstr "Anneau"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:523
msgid ""
"(Personality +15, Intellect +15, Regenerates Hit Points) In the history of the barbarian tribes of Vori, it is rare to find a long reigning chieftain. Rarer still is one who held his position through magic rather than might. Drogg was such--a warrior mage who survived many years of rival challenges. It is said that he wore his helmet, even in sleep. Now that you possess it, you understand why."
msgstr ""
"(Personnalité +15, Intelligence +15, restaure les points de santé) Dans l’histoire des tribus barbares de Vori, un chef ne règne jamais très longtemps. Rare est d’en trouver un qui ait tenu son rang par la magie plutôt que par la force. Drogg était l’un d’eux. Mage guerrier, il survécut de longues années aux défis de ses rivaux. On raconte qu’il portait son casque même lorsqu’il dormait. Vous comprenez pourquoi maintenant."

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1337 assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:523
msgid "Artifact Helm"
msgstr "Heaume"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:523
msgid "Drogg's Helm"
msgstr "Heaume de Drogg"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:524
msgid ""
"(Intellect +50, of Dark Magic, Lich) So named by its creator and only sovereign wearer, Mederon, the first and last Lich Emperor of Nighon. The everlasting dynasty he hoped to found lasted barely a dozen years. Mederon escaped the fate of his kingdom. It is said he still lives as a madman and searches the world for his lost crown."
msgstr ""
"(Intelligence +50, de magie de l’Ombre, Liche) Ainsi nommé par son seul créateur et porteur souverain, Mederon, premier et dernier Empereur liche de Nighon. La dynastie éternelle qu’il espérait fonder dura à peine une douzaine d’années. Mederon échappa au sort de son royaume. Encore en vie mais fou, paraît-il, il chercherait dans le monde entier sa couronne perdue."

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:524
msgid "Artifact Crown"
msgstr "Couronne"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:524
msgid "Crown of Final Dominion"
msgstr "Couronne du dominion final"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:525
msgid ""
"(Feather Falling, Intellect + 30, All magic resistances + 10) When Angels fall from grace, they lose their wings. Since this is an event of extreme infrequency, angel wings are a very rare commodity. Archangel wings are almost never seen. When used as a material, they imbue the resulting item with fantastic powers."
msgstr ""
"(Poids plume, Intelligence +30, protection contre toutes les magies +10) Quand les anges tombent en disgrâce, ils perdent leurs ailes. Comme cela arrive extrêmement peu souvent, les ailes d’ange sont très rares. En particulier, les ailes d’archange. Utilisées comme matériau, elles dotent l’objet fabriqué de pouvoirs fantastiques."

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:525
msgid "Archangel Wings"
msgstr "Ailes d’archange"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1335 assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:525
msgid "Artifact Cloak"
msgstr "Cape"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:526
msgid ""
"(Slows target, Water Resistance -50, Personality -15) The pommel of this sword is gruesomely butted by a shrunken medusa's head. Though greatly diminished, the medusa's power flows along Snake's blade and into its targets--a good design, but poorly implemented, for some of the negative energies flow into the sword's wielder as well."
msgstr ""
"(Ralentit la cible, Protection contre l’Eau -50, Personnalité -15) La garde de cette épée est sinistrement dotée d’une tête de méduse miniature. La méduse est fortement rétrécie. Pourtant, son pouvoir circule dans la lame du Serpent et dans sa cible. Cette conception est ingénieuse mais mal appliquée. En effet, une partie des énergies négatives passe aussi dans celui qui manie l’épée."

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:526 assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:527
msgid "Relic Longsword"
msgstr "Epée"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:526
msgid "Snake"
msgstr "Serpent"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:527
msgid ""
"(Speed +70, Accuracy +70, Armor Class -20) Havoc's enchantment makes it able to readily defeat any target's defenses. Unfortunately, its aggressive spirit makes it indifferent to parrying movements."
msgstr ""
"(Vitesse +70, Précision +70, Classe d’armure -20) L’enchantement Ravages permet de vaincre facilement les défenses de n’importe quelle cible. Malheureusement, son esprit agressif l’empêche de parer les mouvements."

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:527
msgid "Havoc"
msgstr "Ravages"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:528
msgid ""
"(10-20 points of Fire damage, Slow, Speed -20) When the arch assassin, Demetri Razen was finally brought to justice, it was found that his skin was granted unusual hardness by a permanent enchantment. Normal blades would not cut him, so Finality was forged to deliver the death blow sentenced by the Enrothian courts."
msgstr ""
"(10-20 points de dégâts du Feu, Lent, Vitesse -20) La comparution du grand assassin, Demetri Razen, devant la justice révéla qu’un enchantement permanent donnait à sa peau une dureté inhabituelle. Aucune lame normale ne pouvait le blesser. Finalité fut alors forgée pour lui asséner le coup de grâce auquel l’avaient condamné les tribunaux d’Enroth."

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:528
msgid "Finality"
msgstr "Finalité"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:528
msgid "Relic Two-Handed Sword"
msgstr "Epée à deux mains"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:529
msgid ""
"(Might + 70, Accuracy +70, Personality -50, Intellect -50) So called because of its power to demonize its wielder, nevertheless, there are many who would willingly pay the price for the power offered by \"Hell's Cleaver.\""
msgstr ""
"(Force +70, Précision +70, Personnalité -50, Intelligence -50) Le “ Couperet de l’enfer ” est ainsi nommé en raison de son pouvoir à ensorceler son utilisateur. Pourtant, beaucoup seraient prêts à payer cher pour un tel pouvoir."

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:529
msgid "Hell's Cleaver"
msgstr "Couperet de l’enfer"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:529
msgid "Relic Axe"
msgstr "Hache"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:53
msgid "Labyrinth Grapple"
msgstr "Grappin de labyrinthe"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:53
msgid ""
"Minotaurs have very little tolerance for intruders in their hallowed mazes. This fact is well evidenced in the attention paid to weapons constructed for the labyrinth guards."
msgstr ""
"Les minotaures tolèrent très mal les intrus dans leurs dédales sacrés. Un fait le prouve : l’attention qu’ils accordent aux armes fabriquées pour les gardes des labyrinthes."

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:530
msgid ""
"(Vampiric, Might +50, Luck -40) Many under the rule of Luthiner the Severe saw the existence of his spear Spiritslayer as proof of the existence of evil. The injuries caused by the spear go beyond the physical as Spiritslayer takes a strike as an opportunity to drink its target's very essence."
msgstr ""
"(Vampirique, Force +50, Chance -40) Sous le règne de Luthiner le sévère, beaucoup considéraient l’existence de sa lance Tueur d’esprits comme la preuve de l’existence du mal. Les blessures infligées par la lance vont au-delà du physique car Tueur d’esprits profite de chaque coup pour absorber l’essence même de sa cible."

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:530 assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:531
msgid "Relic Spear"
msgstr "Lance"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:530
msgid "Spiritslayer"
msgstr "Tueur d’esprits"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:531
msgid ""
"(Water Breathing, +70 Water Resistance, -70 Fire Resistance) The Trident of Rulership was never meant to be on dry land, yet when the once mighty, ocean to ocean, Triton empire collapsed, many of its greatest artifacts including those of its royal treasure were looted and made their way to the surface."
msgstr ""
"(Respiration sous-marine, +70 Protection contre l’Eau, -70 Protection contre le Feu) Le Trident de souveraineté n’était pas destiné pour la terre ferme. Pourtant, après l’effondrement du puissant empire Triton reliant un océan à l’autre, bon nombre de ses objets les plus prestigieux, y compris le trésor royal, ont été volés et sont remontés à la surface."

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:531
msgid "Trident of Rulership"
msgstr "Trident de souveraineté"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:532
msgid ""
"(Might +40, 4-10 points Electrical damage, Accuracy -40, Necromancer) Though generally considered unfashionable among current necromantic customs, live sacrifice was once widely practiced. To reduce the cruelty inflicted on his victims, the Necromancer Ferredine the Merciful created a blade capable of bringing about a quicker and less suffered end."
msgstr ""
"(Force +40, 4-10 points de dégâts de l’électricité, Précision -40, Nécromancien) Les coutumes nécromanciennes actuelles le considèrent plutôt archaïque, mais le sacrifice d’êtres vivants était jadis beaucoup pratiqué. Pour réduire la cruauté infligée à ses victimes, le nécromancien Ferredine le miséricordieux créa une lame capable de donner une mort plus rapide et moins douloureuse."

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:532
msgid "Blade of Mercy"
msgstr "Lame de la pitié"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:532
msgid "Relic Dagger"
msgstr "Dague"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:533
msgid ""
"(of Air Magic, of Fire Magic, of Water Magic, of Earth Magic, -40 Armor Class) By imposing upon its wielder a deepened state of concentration, the Staff of Elements increases his or her affinity with elemental magic to a profound degree. Of course, it is not always a good thing to have one's attention taken away from one's immediate concerns."
msgstr ""
"(de la Magie de l’Air, de la Magie du Feu, de la Magie de l’Eau, de la Magie de la Terre, -40 Classe d’armure) En imposant à celui qui le manie un état de concentration plus profonde, le Bâton des élémentaires infuse une connaissance accrue de la magie élémentaire. Bien entendu, il n’est pas toujours bon de détourner son attention des préoccupations immédiates."

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:533
msgid "Relic Staff"
msgstr "Bâton"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:533
msgid "Staff of Elements"
msgstr "Bâton des élémentaires"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:534
msgid ""
"(Accuracy +100, Bow skill + 5, Armor Class -20) This bow was built to the specifications of the great Elven tournament archer, Terin Tourfeather. More concerned with fancy shooting than with the realities of the battlefield, the bow's detrimental effects were of no concern to Tourfeather--more workaday wielders should pay more heed."
msgstr ""
"(Précision +100, compétence Arc +5, Classe d’armure -20) Cet arc fut fabriqué selon les spécifications du grand archer de tournoi elfique, Terin Tourfeather. Plus intéressé par le tir de fantaisie que par les réalités du champ de bataille, Tourfeather ne se souciait guère des effets négatifs de l’arc : les archers plus ordinaires devraient se méfier davantage."

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:534
msgid "Relic Bow"
msgstr "Arc"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:534
msgid "Tournament Bow"
msgstr "Arc de tournoi"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:535
msgid ""
"(Swift, Accuracy -50, Dark Elf) An ingenious combination of the mechanical and magical went into the creation of this self-cocking crossbow which launches its quarrels with incredible force. That the same launching force causes it to kick like a mule means only the most skilled can use it to any good effect."
msgstr ""
"(Rapidité, Précision -50, Elfe de l’Ombre) Cette arbalète est issue d’une combinaison ingénieuse de la mécanique et de la magie. Elle se tend automatiquement et lance ses flèches avec une force incroyable. Cependant, cette force de lancement la fait ruer comme une mule. Par conséquent, seuls les plus compétents peuvent l’utiliser de façon avantageuse."

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:535
msgid "Lightning Crossbow"
msgstr "Arbalète éclair"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:535
msgid "Relic Crossbow"
msgstr "Arbalète"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:536
msgid ""
"(Personality +80, Intellect +70, -30 Mind and Spirit resistances) The final stage of degeneration from their human form leaves a Lich completely soulless and thus immune to certain magics. Such liches often curse their personal items with vulnerabilities to these magics to dissuade others from using them."
msgstr ""
"(Personnalité +80, Intelligence +70, -30 Protection contre l’Esprit et le Spiritisme) La phase finale de dégénérescence de leur forme humaine laisse les liches totalement vides d’âme, et donc immunisées contre certaines magies. Ces liches infligent souvent des malédictions à leurs objets personnels pour les rendre vulnérables et dissuader les autres de les utiliser."

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:536
msgid "Last Stage Cuirass"
msgstr "Cuirasse de phase finale"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:536
msgid "Relic Leather Armor"
msgstr "Armure en cuir"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:537
msgid ""
"(Immune to Fear, Stone, Paralysis, and Sleep; Personality -15, Luck -15) The great knight Gerrald Herondale abandoned this shield after it took the brunt of a dark and deadly curse. Though it still retained its great powers, the shield was also weighed down with malevolent energies."
msgstr ""
"(Immunise contre la peur, la pierre, la paralysie et le sommeil ; Personnalité -15, Chance -15) Le grand chevalier Gerrald Herondale abandonna ce bouclier à la suite du choc d’une malédiction sinistre et mortelle. Le bouclier conserva ses grands pouvoirs, mais fut aussi chargé d’énergies maléfiques."

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:537
msgid "Herondale's Lost Shield"
msgstr "Bouclier perdu d’Herondale"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:537
msgid "Relic Small Shield"
msgstr "Petit bouclier"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:538
msgid ""
"(of Water, Alchemy skill + 5, Intellect +40, Endurance -20) A lost relic of the Freehaven Alchemists' Guild, until its disappearance, this ring was the signet of the guildmaster. It was meant to be worn only during the mixing of the most powerful potions for it drew much energy from the user."
msgstr ""
"(de l’Eau, compétence Alchimie +5, Intelligence +40, Endurance -20) Relique perdue de la Guilde des alchimistes de Freehaven, cet anneau fut jusqu’à sa disparition le sceau du maître de la guilde. Conçu pour être porté uniquement pendant la préparation des potions les plus puissantes, il puisait beaucoup d’énergie dans l’utilisateur."

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:538
msgid "Relic Ring"
msgstr "Anneau"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:538
msgid "Ring of Fusion"
msgstr "Anneau de fusion"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:539
msgid ""
"(Luck + 90, Personality -50) The only reason someone would wear this hat is for the luck it conveys. It is the farthest thing from flattering!"
msgstr ""
"(Chance +90, Personnalité -50) La seule raison valable de porter ce chapeau, c’est qu’il porte chance. Il est loin d’être élégant !"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:539
msgid "Lucky Hat"
msgstr "Chapeau porte-bonheur"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:539
msgid "Relic Hat"
msgstr "Chapeau"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:54
msgid "Hayfork"
msgstr "Fourche à foin"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:54
msgid ""
"Though a common farming implement, this hayfork is of sturdy construction and could be an excellent, if improvised, weapon."
msgstr ""
"Simple outil agricole, cette fourche à foin est toutefois solide et pourrait s’avérer au besoin une arme excellente."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1644 assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1645 assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1646
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:54 assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:55 assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:56
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:57 assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:58 assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:844
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:845 assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:846
msgid "Trident"
msgstr "Trident"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:540
msgid ""
"(Might +100, Immune to Fear, Accuracy -30, Armor Class -15) An experiment of the Blackshire Artificers' Guild, this belt was designed to turn its wearer into the perfect warrior--mighty and fearless. No more were made when in field tests it became apparent that \"foolhardy\" and \"careless\" were not virtues of the perfect warrior."
msgstr ""
"(Force +100, Immunise contre la peur, Précision -30, Classe d’armure -15) Expérience de la Guilde des artificiers de Blackshire, cette ceinture a été conçue pour faire de celui qui la porte le parfait guerrier, puissant et courageux. Mais les essais sur le terrain ont révélé que “ téméraire ” et “ inconsidéré ” n’étaient pas les vertus du parfait guerrier. On arrêta alors d’en fabriquer."

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:540
msgid "Berserker Belt"
msgstr "Ceinture de fou furieux"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:540
msgid "Relic Belt"
msgstr "Ceinture"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:541
msgid "Special Mace"
msgstr "Masse"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:541
msgid ""
"Though at first it appears to be the same type of mace carried by Sun Temple clerics everywhere, this item seems to thrum with conflicting energies."
msgstr ""
"Au premier abord, on pourrait croire qu’il s’agit du même type de masse porté partout par les clercs du Temple du Soleil. Pourtant, cet objet semble vibrer d’énergies contradictoires."

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:542
msgid ""
"Quest Item: Charles Quixote's personal spear of Dragon slaying, Ebonest is a fine weapon indeed. When used against a Dragon, it seems to aim unerringly for the chinks between its target's tough scales."
msgstr ""
"Objet de quête : lance personnelle de Charles Quixote destinée à massacrer les dragons, Ebonest est sans aucun doute une très bonne arme. Contre un dragon, elle semble viser sans faute les fentes entre les écailles dures de sa cible."

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:542
msgid "Special Spear"
msgstr "Lance"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:543
msgid ""
"Quest Item: That the Whistlebones would settle upon such a fierce weapon for their heirloom speaks much of their commitment to the family business of Dragon hunting."
msgstr ""
"Objet de quête : que les Whistlebone choisissent une arme aussi redoutable en guise d’héritage en dit long sur leur engagement dans l’activité familiale de la chasse aux dragons."

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:543
msgid "Special Two-Handed Sword"
msgstr "Epée à deux mains"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:543
msgid "Sword of Whistlebone"
msgstr "Epée de Whistlebone"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:544
msgid ""
"Quest Item: No Minotaur kings wear a crown. Instead as their badge of office they carry great axes of the finest workmanship. This axe was lost when Balthazar was betrayed by the Vori Frost Giants. That it is strongly enchanted is clear; when used in battle its blows deliver both normal damage and impart a numbing bite of freezing cold."
msgstr ""
"Objet de quête : aucun roi minotaure ne porte de couronne. A la place, ils portent, en guise de signe de fonction, de grandes haches d’excellente qualité. Cette hache fut perdue au moment où Balthazar fut trahi par les géants du Gel de Vori. Dotée d’un puissant enchantement, elle porte des coups provoquant des dégâts habituels et inflige en plus une morsure de gel paralysante."

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1354 assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:544
msgid "Special Two-Handed Axe"
msgstr "Hache à deux mains"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:545
msgid ""
"Bows of Kreegan bone are highly sought after; the material is strong and takes enchantments easily. The most sought after bone comes from Kreegans of the devil race's former ruling class."
msgstr ""
"Très recherchés, les arcs en os kreegans sont solides et intègrent facilement les enchantements. L’os le plus recherché est celui des Kreegans de l’ancienne classe dirigeante de la race des démons."

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:545
msgid "Noblebone Bow"
msgstr "Arc en os noble"

# imported from FR (MMMerge localization)
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1347 assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:1348 assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:545
msgid "Special Bow"
msgstr "Arc"

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:546
msgid ""
"(Shared life, Endurance + 20) A ring of simple metal (copper or brass?), warm on touch."
msgstr ""
"(Partage de vie, + 20 d'Endurance) Un anneau de métal ordinaire (cuivre ou laiton ?), chaud au toucher."

# machine translation (Claude), review
#: assets_dev/engine/data_tables/items.txt:546
